{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/496712-recommended-reading-for-werewolf","id":496712,"title":"Recommended Reading for Werewolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-29T13:39:17-07:00","id":496712,"title":"Recommended Reading for Werewolf","content":"I'm not a big werewolf fan outside of Werewolf the Forsaken. I've seen movies, but never really been that impressed, I read some books a long time ago but they're fairly forgettable. In fact before Forsaken, Werewolf was probably the least interesting line of the World of Darkness to me. Still, when I was getting ready for second edition I decided to find a book or two about werewolves to put me in the mood and I stumbled across <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Autobiography-Werewolf-Hunter-Brian-Easton-ebook/dp/B003TU2IV2/\" target=\"_blank\">Autobiography of a Werewolf Hunter</a>. It's from Permuted Press, which seems to publish supernatural post apocalypses and books about monster hunters, and I wasn't expecting much. Technically it's not even about werewolves, the focus is clearly on the werewolf hunter.<br /> <br /> But it's a fantastic book. And I've been sick lately, which is why I've been posting so much, and the last book in the trilogy came out so with my downtime I've gotten through it and I have to heartily recommend it.<br /> <br /> With one major caveat.<br /> <br /> The book and its two sequels are very well written, the author seems to take into account a wide variety of werewolf legends, and though this seems to be his first full length work it's fantastic. But a lot of people might be turned off by the content, because the werewolf hunter is fairly hardcore. He has his good sides, especially in the first book, but when it comes down to him versus werewolves he's like the Punisher. There is no compromise, no give. To him, werewolves are personifications of absolute evil, blasphemies on Earth.<br /> <br /> And the thing is, he's right. These werewolves aren't the Forsaken, and they put the Pure to shame. They are Evil with a capital E and a cruel accent and a bunch of l's and a maniacal cackle echoing in the background as it's said. So between him being a hardcore hunter, and them being evil, the books can get pretty grim and dark. Still, if one is looking for inspiration for evil werewolves, it's probably the best source out there, as the wolves have their own culture and beliefs and notable individuals.<br /> <br /> If any of you end up reading it I'm sure you'll like it.<br /> <br /> Any questions, feel free to ask. I was thinking about just talking briefly about the werewolves in case people aren't interested in reading an entire trilogy to find out about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-29-2015, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T14:24:11-07:00","id":496756,"title":"","content":"I might heartily suggest the mammoth book of wolfmen. Short story anthology by horror novelists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T14:59:46-07:00","id":496802,"title":"","content":"Once again I will recommend Linda Godfrey's <i>Real Wolfmen: True Encounters in Modern America</i> as a source of ideas. Just take a sighting from the book and figure out what the werewolves were up to. As an added bonus, some of Linda's theories on the nature of the wolfmen make for great setting hacks if you want to do something different than the usual animism/spirit related werewolves of the WoD, one of those theories is even the basis for how werewolves work in a novel I am writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T20:14:15-07:00","id":497025,"title":"","content":"Taking notes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T21:15:56-07:00","id":497072,"title":"","content":"Just In case Sikla is reading this, One of the werewolves in Linda's book said the syllables Gar-dar-rah to the witness.<br /> Just for the sake of seeing if i have a story hook here, would that mean anything in First Tongue?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T21:23:53-07:00","id":497076,"title":"","content":"My recommendations are The Wolf's Hour and The Hunter from the Woods. The first is a story about a Russian werewolf turned English spy that works to stop a Nazi plot before D Day. The werewolves are obviously different from W:tF Uratha but it's a fantastic look at the instincts of a werewolf, some neat uses of the wolf form and the flashback scenes to his life in Russia is fantastic. The second is a collection of short stories about the character from The Wolf's Hour throughout his life and is also a fantastic read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T22:26:08-07:00","id":497101,"title":"","content":"Something a little different and which may not be for everybody but is one thing I know with a werewolf protagonist and I quite liked was <i>Dance in the Vampire Bund</i>, which is a manga (there is also an anime adaptation of it).<br /> <br /> Whilst on the subject, my very first Werewolf character was a Rahu Blood Talon based off The Captain, a mute werewolf BAMF from the manga <i>Hellsing</i>. However in that he was the only one of his kind, however in his final fight scene he demonstrated a really good show of a part spirit looking Gauru form. As <i>Hellsing</i> now has a 10-part licenced OVA form based off the manga, the tenth and last episode may be worth checking out to see him go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T22:37:10-07:00","id":497106,"title":"","content":"I have read a couple of werewolf novels in my life and most seem cheesy to me. Like &quot;The Wolf Gift&quot; and its sequel by Anne Rice were a total disappointment. I really had high hopes for this series but it ended up popping in my face. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Note: she should just stick with her vampires.<br /> <br /> Right now I'm reading &quot;Wagner the Werewolf&quot; by George Reynolds. It's a classic werewolf literature so I'm hoping I get something good. So far it's okay, so far....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T07:41:10-07:00","id":497441,"title":"","content":"Bitten and Stolen, the first two books of the Women of the Otherworld series, by Kelly Armstrong. Great example of werewolves.<br /> <br /> The basic idea is that the main character, Elena, was bitten and turned into a werewolf. There are born werewolves, but only males can inherit the gene. Werewolves usually bite people for the express purpose of killing them, and even if they don't, there's a pretty slim chance of surviving the bite, so Elena is the ONLY female werewolf in existence. At the start of the first book, she's left the Pack, and is trying to live a normal life, which is difficult when you HAVE to go out and change into a werewolf every week or so. She gets called back to help the Pack out with a serious problem.<br /> <br /> The Pack is a relatively small group of werewolves, but they are THE authority over all werewolves. There are many non-Pack werewolves, called mutts, and the Pack makes sure they don't draw attention to werewolves in general, and keep them on their toes (one of many rules: only Pack werewolves are allowed to claim territory.) Some great scenes about werewolves hunting, and the kind of family dynamic a Pack has. Particularly interesting, I think, is the character of Clay, who was bitten as a young boy and lived completely feral in the swamps of Louisiana until Jeremy, the current Pack Alpha, found him. Clay has a genius-level IQ and a degree in anthropology, specializing in anthropomorphic religions. He also has no clue about most human behavior, and doesn't care to blend in most of the time. Really fascinating character concept.<br /> <br /> It's definitely in the &quot;urban fantasy/paranormal romance&quot; genre, so that might turn some folks off, but for my money, it's the best werewolf fiction I've read recently. The sequel, Stolen, opens up the world, adding in other supernaturals and asking the question &quot;what would happen if a rich eccentric computer/video game dude funded a group of parapsychologists.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T09:38:46-07:00","id":497536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/496712-recommended-reading-for-werewolf?p=497072#post497072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just In case Sikla is reading this, One of the werewolves in Linda's book said the syllables Gar-dar-rah to the witness.<br /> Just for the sake of seeing if i have a story hook here, would that mean anything in First Tongue?</div> </div> </div> </div>GAH! Why didn't I see this before?<br /> <br /> Gar-dar-rah...hmmm. It could mean a number of things, but I've heard the gar-dar-rah story before. My best best is that it's a corruption of the word &quot;Urfarah&quot;, with the werewolf probably the equivalent of, &quot;God!&quot; at being spotted WITHOUT lunacy happening, or it's roughly &quot;flee-kill-beat&quot;, which might translate to, &quot;Get out of here before I beat you to death, meatsack!&quot;<br /> <br /> On that note, I also second Linda's work. She's got a lot of good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T10:31:31-07:00","id":497624,"title":"","content":"Breeds is a relatively recent horror novel that's pretty brutal. <br /> <br /> Also the howling","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T14:27:59-07:00","id":497883,"title":"","content":"I will suggest the graphic novel Welcome to Hoxford. Its about a pack of werewolves that run a prison. Its a quick read and very worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T15:59:14-07:00","id":497955,"title":"","content":"That is a thing I bought and liked. Also The Pack, which is a graphic novel set in ancient egypt. Buyable on the amazon kindle. I may also recommend Steven Wedel's Shara and Ulrik books. I might also recommend his Nadia's Children, but the book felt a bit off compared to the previous two. He writes werewolf very well (as an ap english instructor I would hope so!) and Shara is especially good at capturing that &quot;Pup's first time in the woods&quot; feeling. It also covers the inter species breeding thing, which may shock some of you but he does it with a naturalist style and less a religiously moral one. His books definitely cement the werewolf as being &quot;neither human nor wolf.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}